OL,3,A'What you see is what you pay' - why
OL,4,Asome US restaurants are banning tips
OL,5,
OL,6,FWine waiter Caroline Kraetzer earns $40
OL,7,F(#30) an hour, double what most service
OL,8,Fstaff in San Francisco are paid but
OL,9,Fthen it costs a lot to eat at her
OL,10,Frestaurant.
OL,12,FAt a set price of $140 (#100) per
OL,13,Fperson, La Cigale is one of a small
OL,14,Fnumber of restaurants charging higher
OL,15,Fprices so it can pay high salaries -
OL,16,Fand it doesn't allow tips.
OL,18,FIt tells customers: "What you see is
OL,19,Fwhat you pay. We do not accept tips,
OL,20,Fyour kind words and return visits will
OL,21,Fsuffice."
OL,23,APub: 24-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
